      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Volume types",
      "items": [
        "gp3 starts at 3,000 IOPS and 125 MiB/s, tunable regardless of size",
        "io1 and io2 target transactional workloads needing hundreds of thousands of IOPS",
        "st1 and sc1 are low-cost HDD options for sequential throughput"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "StorageClass configuration",
      "items": [
        "Default to provisioner: ebs.csi.aws.com, type: gp3, encrypted: \"true\"",
        "volumeBindingMode: WaitForFirstConsumer creates the volume in the AZ where the pod lands",
        "Setting allowVolumeExpansion: true keeps online expansion available later"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Best practices",
      "items": [
        "An EBS volume is a single-AZ resource, so a pod moved to another AZ cannot mount it",
        "Give the driver a least-privilege IAM role through IRSA or Pod Identity",
        "Back up with snapshots and rehearse recovery through CSI VolumeSnapshot"
      ]
    }
